===== NEW   =====
The numbers are almost comic. In the American Civil War, Army surgeons wrote down 246 ,712 battle wounds. Exactly 922 came from a blade or bayonet, and of those, 56 killed the man. They kept it on the end of the rifle anyway for another 200 years, not for the men it killed, for the men who saw it coming and decided not to be there.
